==English==

===Noun===
{{en-noun|affidavit men}}

# {{lb|en|archaic|or|historical}} A man who (in the 1700s or 1800s) loitered around courts, offering to bear [[false witness]].
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1742|title=Proceedings of the Political Club &c|journal=The London Magazine|month=January|page=222
|passage=We know how easy it is for Ministers to find '''Affidavit Men''', and no Court in ''England'' could give the Gentleman any Redress, because the Search was every Night made according to the express Directions of an Act of Parliament. {{...}} no Man could say, the '''Affidavit Man''' had taken a false Oath, when he swore he had Reason to suspect, that Seamen would be that night concealed in such a House; {{...}}}}

